  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Constructing the Backend**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the `server.ts` backend file. I plan to instantiate `@google/genai` using `import { GoogleGenAI } from \"@google/genai\";`. My intent is to use `gemini-3.5-flash` for the standard tasks, such as summaries, formatting, and interview evaluation, and leverage search grounding for company-specific tasks.\n\n\n**Refining the API Endpoints**\n\nI\'ve been refining the API endpoint handlers for `server.ts`. I plan to send requests in JSON format for clarity. I\'m focusing on defining POST endpoints for `/api/optimize-cv`, `/api/generate-cover-letter`, `/api/generate-networking`, `/api/interview-simulator`, and `/api/interview-evaluate`. Each will receive specific data and return structured JSON responses, aligning with the type definitions in `lib/types.ts`. I want to ensure robust error handling and structured outputs. I\'m thinking I\'ll use the flash model for all the endpoints, including search grounding, with the tool configuration.\n\n\n**Implementing the Dossier Endpoint**\n\nI\'m now implementing the `/api/company-dossier` endpoint within `server.ts`. It will accept `companyName` and `role` as input, returning a `CompanyDossierResult`. I\'m focusing on search-grounded research for this. I\'ve also integrated lazy initialization for the Gemini client, including an error guard for the API key. The plan is to catch errors for missing keys. I\'m focusing on ensuring clear JSON schema results, and appropriate guardrails.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will now write the full-stack `/server.ts` file. It will handle our backend career API endpoints (`/api/optimize-cv`, `/api/generate-cover-letter`, `/api/generate-networking`, `/api/interview-simulator`, `/api/interview-evaluate`, and `/api/company-dossier`) by making backend calls to the Gemini API, using lazy initialization as per our safety rules. It also configures Express, parses JSON payloads, and handles development vs. production static and SPA serving."
