  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Optimization Triggers**\n\nI\'m focusing on `/src/components/CVOptimizer.tsx`. I\'ve started examining the UI requirements for optimization features. Specifically, I\'m focusing on the Gupy Optimization Active Trigger \342\200\223 a checkbox or similar toggle element. This will allow the user to activate resume optimization for passing \"robos,\" or automated resume scanners, which seems to be a popular request.\n\n\n**Implementing Gupy-Specific Fields**\n\nI\'m expanding the `/src/components/CVOptimizer.tsx` component. I\'m adding a card-style trigger with state variables `optimizeForGupy` and `setOptimizeForGupy`. I\'m also including an input field for the user to enter a job URL or title, using `jobUrlOrTitle` and `setJobUrlOrTitle` states, to allow them to indicate \"Vaga Encontrada na Internet (URL ou T\303\255tulo)\". I\'ve integrated these new states into the POST request body.\n\n\n**Refining UI Placement**\n\nI\'m now refining the placement of the Gupy Optimization fields within the input panel. I\'m aiming for a clear chronological flow: Job Description input first, followed by the optional job URL, and then the Gupy optimization trigger. After the user provides the inputs, they will be able to \"Alinhar Curr\303\255culo \303\240 Vaga\". I\'m also considering how to display the Gupy compatibility score and advice within the output panel, potentially using progress indicators.\n\n\n**Displaying Compatibility Score**\n\nI\'m now integrating the Gupy compatibility score display into the output panel. I\'m focusing on a visually appealing presentation, using a card-style UI element to highlight the score. It\'ll include a percentage value, a brief explanation of Gupy\'s semantic engines, and advice. I\'m working with a design using Tailwind classes, with indigo and emerald color theming, and appropriate spacing.\n\n\n**Enhancing Result Display**\n\nI\'m now integrating live insights from internet vacancy searches into the output. I\'m focusing on displaying this information alongside the checklist. I\'m building out a conditional render that will display a div when `internetVagaSearchInfo` is present and not empty. I\'m using a sky-themed visual style, using Tailwind classes with the intention to maintain a good visual separation. I\'m working to show a card-style UI element to highlight the advice.\n\n\n**Refining Insight Display**\n\nI\'m now refining the display of internet vacancy search insights. I\'m focusing on ensuring it\'s visually distinct. I\'ve integrated a new component, which displays a heading \"Insights da Vaga Buscada na Internet\" with a sky-themed styling to maintain clear visual separation. This section uses a small filled circle and concise text to improve the presentation of the insights. I\'m focusing on the `CVOptimizer.tsx` file for these updates.\n\n\n"
