ypes. This includes `experience`, `education`, and `skills` now. I\'m making sure these fields will be properly parsed, from the various inputs from the users.\n\n\n**Implementing Error Handling**\n\nI\'ve been working on robust error handling for the parsing function. Now I\'m focusing on parsing the output from Gemini, with try-catch blocks to handle potential issues with the JSON response from the AI. If the JSON is invalid, a structured fallback is returned, that includes default values and an error message, which increases the robustness of the system. I will test the fallback with various resume inputs.\n\n\n**Integrating the Resume Upload**\n\nI\'m now integrating the resume upload functionality. I\'m focusing on the frontend, specifically creating a drag-and-drop file upload component for the `ResumeForm.tsx`. I will make it work with both PDF and docx file formats. The upload will be used to automatically categorize and pre-fill data.\n\n\n"
