  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Mapping the Imports**\n\nOkay, I\'m mapping out the necessary imports for updating `/src/components/ResumeForm.tsx`. It looks like I need `Plus`, `Trash2`, `Edit2`, `Check`, `User`, `Briefcase`, `GraduationCap`, `Code`, `Languages`, and `FileText`. I\'m going for an elegant approach to this modification.\n\n\n**Expanding the Imports**\n\nOkay, I\'ve expanded the import statements in `/src/components/ResumeForm.tsx`. I\'ve added `UploadCloud`, `Download`, `FileCode`, `AlertCircle`, and `Loader2` to the import list from \"lucide-react.\" Now, I\'m working on the states and methods for the upload functionality, before the return statement. I\'m focusing on drag-and-drop file handling, background uploading, and download implementations.\n\n\n**Implementing Drag-and-Drop**\n\nI\'m now integrating drag-and-drop file handling. I\'ve defined `dragActive` and `setDragActive` to manage the drag state. My `handleDrag` function updates this state based on drag events. I\'m focusing now on implementing file processing with a `processFile` method, setting the uploading state, and error handling.\n\n\n**Processing the File**\n\nI\'ve got the file processing logic almost complete. My focus is on handling file reading as base64, then sending that, the MIME type, and file name to an API endpoint (`/api/parse-cv-file`). Error handling is critical here. I\'m checking for server errors and specific API key missing errors to ensure robust feedback. On a success, I\'ll `onChange` with parsed data.\n\n\n**Refining the Error Handling**\n\nI\'m now refining the error-handling within the `processFile` function. I\'ve added robust checks within the `try...catch...finally` block to catch and display more specific error messages to the user. I\'m ensuring that any issues during file processing, such as reading, sending, or parsing, are caught and handled gracefully, setting the `uploadError` state accordingly, and that any issues will also be reported to the console. Finally, I\'ve added a check to handle missing API keys.\n\n\n**Generating the Markdown**\n\nI\'m now generating the Markdown content. I\'ve begun crafting the structure and content for the resume, focusing on the contact information, professional profile, experience, and education sections. I\'m adding section headers, using appropriate formatting for roles, companies, dates, locations, and descriptions. My goal is to produce clean and well-structured Markdown.\n\n\n**Structuring the Markdown**\n\nI\'m now focusing on adding education, skills, and languages sections to the markdown. I\'m dynamically generating these from the `cvData` object. I am iterating through each section, mapping data to appropriate markdown formatting and using a clean structure. I\'m prioritizing readability and maintainability of the markdown output. I am also working on generating the final output for the download.\n\n\n\n**Consolidating the Layout**\n\nI\'m now consolidating the file upload and download widget design. I\'ve decided to arrange the \"Templates Selector\" and \"File Upload Widget\" within a grid or vertically to maximize usability. On a desktop, I\'m thinking of a two-card layout, or a refined single section of \"Import & Intelligent Upload\" with two parallel cards. The left card will house the drag-and-drop file uploader, featuring a premium style, and the right card, the templates selector and download button.\n\n\n**Refining the UI**\n\nI\'m now refining the UI for the intelligent upload feature, focusing on the left-side card. I\'ve integrated a card layout within the designated container, incorporating the upload icon and descriptive text. I\'m focusing on text alignment and whitespace for a clean appearance. I am implementing the drag-and-drop area now.\n\n\n**Implementing the Drag Zone**\n\nI\'m now implementing the drag-and-drop zone. I\'m building out the `div` with the `drag-drop-zone` ID, including `onDragEnter`, `onDragOver`, `onDragLeave`, and `onDrop` event handlers. I\'m focusing on conditional styling, using `dragActive` to highlight the zone when a file is being dragged over it. I\'m also inserting an invisible file input element to handle file selection, implementing `handleFileChange`.\n\n\n\n**Adding the Status Message**\n\nI\'m now integrating a status message to provide feedback to the user during file processing. I\'m adding conditional rendering to display \"Processing CV with ChatGPT/Gemini...\" when a file upload is in progress. I\'m aiming for a clear and unobtrusive message within the existing UI structure, along with the other relevant information.\n\n\n\n**Integrating the Status**\n\nI\'ve integrated the status message within the upload area, using conditional rendering. I\'m dynamically displaying the appropriate message based on the file processing stage. I\'m focusing on the visual coherence, to ensure it doesn\'t distract from the user\'s workflow. I\'m using a clear and readable style with the alerts.\n\n\n\n**Refining the Imports**\n\nI\'m now refining the import handling for development and administration profiles. I\'m focusing on ensuring proper import logic for each, updating the logic, and testing the behavior to ensure smooth data integration within the resume form.\n\n\n\n**Updating the Download**\n\nI am now focusing on refining the download functionality and style. I\'ve integrated a download button that triggers the `handleDownloadMarkdown` function, which generates and downloads the Markdown content. I\'ve incorporated the `Download` icon from \"lucide-react\" for enhanced visual appeal and usability. I have also changed the button to green.\n\n\n\n"
