g the user can easily add and manage multiple entries. I\'m prioritizing the \"+ Adicionar Cargo\" button\'s visibility and clarity, and I will add an experience count indicator for intuitive display. I\'m also now reviewing `ResumeForm.tsx` to ensure unlimited additions are supported and to identify any visual or code limitations.\n\n\n**Enhancing UX Clarity**\n\nI\'m now prioritizing UX enhancements for experience management. I will add clear labels like \"Experi\303\252ncia / Cargo #{idx + 1}\" to each entry, making it obvious the list is dynamic. I\'m also considering \"Limpar\", \"Duplicar\" or another \"+ Adicionar Experi\303\252ncia / Cargo\" button at the bottom of the list for easy access, since many users look there. I\'m now looking at `ResumeForm.tsx` to check for implementation possibilities.\n\n\n**Implementing Bottom Addition**\n\nI\'m now implementing the \"+ Adicionar Nova Experi\303\252ncia Profissional\" button card at the bottom of the experience list and the same for education. This will clarify that they can add multiple entries. I\'m focusing on the visual cues to make the experience addition intuitive. The goal is to make it effortless for the user to add as many experiences as they want!\n\n\n"
